# END GENERATED node-llama-cpp dependency closure

# Kept variants: win-x64 (CPU fallback) and win-x64-vulkan (the GPU backend
# this machine actually uses, per the 0.1 spike's `llama.gpu === "vulkan"`).
#
# NOTE: this ONLY works for un-ignoring variants we want — it does NOT
# reliably keep unwanted variants (win-arm64, win-x64-cuda, win-x64-cuda-ext)
# out. Tried the standard gitignore fix (an explicit re-ignore rule placed
# after this block, since later rules should win) and it had zero effect
# under @vscode/vsce 2.32.0 — two consecutive `npm run package` runs before
# and after adding it produced byte-identical .vsix output. Whatever vsce's
# ignore engine does with negation precedence for a path under an
# already-un-ignored ancestor, it isn't standard gitignore behavior, and
# isn't worth fighting further here. The actual fix for keeping those three
# variants out is `scripts/prune-unused-native-variants.js`, which physically
# deletes them from node_modules before packaging — wired into
# `npm run package`. See that script for the reasoning and the exact list.
!node_modules/@node-llama-cpp
!node_modules/@node-llama-cpp/win-x64
!node_modules/@node-llama-cpp/win-x64/**
!node_modules/@node-llama-cpp/win-x64-vulkan
!node_modules/@node-llama-cpp/win-x64-vulkan/**

